  "details": "Was submitting this for support but found cause ~~\n\nVRchat seems to be unable to decide if i have controllers (vive wands) or not, they work and track perfect in steamVR home and other games (ex Rec room). \n\nBut when used inside VRchat they will track perfectly until i hold them still, then vr chat seems to forget i have controllers and switches to the \"use headset to point a mouse\" input style.\n-----------------------------\nI discovered this was because i had a controller connected and it was acting as input. Perhaps an icon should appear for a second on the screen when you switch input types so you can be aware of what is happening",
